    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301">

                <pb facs="0286" n="276" xml:id="pg276"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/1–2649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Taipei</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Krentz</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-01-26T16:00:00+08:00">January 26, 1949—4
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 26—1:37 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. Reurtel 5.<anchor n="40" xml:id="d301-f1"/> Majority US military equipment
                    remains Keelung dock but local government making effort disperse through island.
                    Railways choked with unloaded cars. No sign plans reship mainland.</p>
                <p>Repeated Nanking as 17.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Krentz</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
